title: Nun (mythology)
description: Ancient Egyptian personification of the primordial watery abyss
hook: "Nun is the water that was there before anything else: the abyss the
  first sunrise had to climb out of, and the god who will one day destroy
  existence and take everything back into it. No cult was ever addressed to
  him."
standfirst: In ancient Egyptian religion, Nun personified the primordial
  watery abyss that existed at the time of creation, and from which the sun
  god Ra arose. One of the eight deities of the Ogdoad, he had no temple and
  no cult, yet was painted on temple walls for the rest of Egyptian religious
  history.
